{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UeQvQc6K8S7XRJcjtfFLVP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty â€” one self-contained folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`), Python stdlib only, plain-markdown source of truth, no database and no external deps (one declared exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals).\n\nWhat it is and does:\n\n- **Task/project manager over markdown.** It reads and writes plain `.md` files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`) as the sole source of truth â€” tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved â†’ Restored, each optionally carrying notes.\n\n- **Ships as a persistent local web app.** `anchor_gui.py` is the primary interface: a stdlib HTTP server bound to `http://localhost:8777`, run as the always-on Windows NSSM service `anchor`, generating the full interactive dashboard HTML on each request. `anchor.py` is a CLI mirror of the same logic that also emits a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Has grown an \"R&D Control Surface\" (v2â†’v4).** Beyond plain tasks, it manages trio-driven R&D projects (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman) per project: session history, cached/validated AI summaries, grass-catcher ideas, pinned deliverables, and effort/cost rollups.\n\n- **Latest layer is the v4 \"Project Cockpit.\"** Each project window is a single-screen cockpit â€” lanes (Research/Planning/Build/Deliverables/Grass) shown as tiles with one honest status light, clicking a tile expands an inline panel (summary on top, real resizable xterm.js terminal below). Terminals are real ConPTY sessions, each git-worktree-isolated, with an engine toggle (Claude/Gemini), and the lane's skill auto-loads and greets exactly once (fixing the old repeating-prompt bug).\n\n- **Self-verifying.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM, parsing every file and exercising every endpoint plus the v2/v3/v4 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed â€” never live `claude`, never the live `:8777` service), writing dated reports and surfacing failures as a dashboard banner.\n\n- **Branded as a Ghost World Labs tool** \"powered by NextGen Nuclear â˜¢,\" using a vendored brand mark.\n\nOne caveat on grounding: the bullets above come from `CLAUDE.md` and the locked design docs, not from re-reading the running code this turn â€” accurate as of the documented v4 merge (commit `38fd70e`, 2026-06-13)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1d004be1-d05f-4a5d-8ba2-43032e324f3d","uuid":"869db036-b0f5-4893-9324-fdc972b81226","request_id":"req_011Cc2J7bG8sXH9XwtAtxWak"}
